{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_aaa8fe19bd4dafbc69eb228575e200902c30a856da7f861ba914161c5d13634c", "title": "LE (rapper)", "text": "Ahn Hyo-jin (born December 10, 1991), better known by her stage name LE ( ), is a South Korean rapper, singer, songwriter, and record producer. She is the main rapper of the K-pop girl group EXID.", "score": 21.2456}, {"id": "hp_doc_8880bd0353beae31226dd8f76aed6a23b3c983f50d2e9efd011c094a47983eb5", "title": "Fugees", "text": "Fugees (sometimes The Fugees; formerly Tranzlator Crew) were an American hip hop group who rose to fame in the early-1990s. Their repertoire included elements of hip hop, soul and Caribbean music, particularly reggae. The members of the group were rapper/singer/producer Wyclef Jean, rapper/singer/producer Lauryn Hill, and rapper/producer Pras Michel. Deriving their name from the term refugee, Jean and Michel are Haitian, while Hill is American.", "score": 12.7366}, {"id": "hp_doc_cf8efa5d9122b18972d22a62668a90fb9bdcb16d6057db528fad915dd5b2f0b6", "title": "Gunplay (rapper)", "text": "Richard Morales, Jr. (born July 18, 1979), better known by his stage name Gunplay, is an American hip hop recording artist from Carol City, Florida. He embarked on his career in hip hop, as a member of fellow Florida-based rapper Rick Ross's southern hip hop group, Triple C's. Triple C's released their debut album, \"Custom Cars & Cycles\", in 2009. After signing to Ross's Maybach Music Group label, upon its inception in 2009, Gunplay would announce he secured a solo recording contract with Def Jam Recordings, in July 2012. He released several mixtapes, such as \"601 & Snort\". His debut studio album, titled \"Living Legend\", was released on July 31, 2015.", "score": 10.1573}], "remaining_searches": 2}
